  "scope": "One managed render-reservation pool across ordinary and linked XYZ viewer surfaces, persisted resource configuration, C++/Python diagnostics and deterministic lifecycle release.",
  "semantics": "Move-only shared-state leases charge working reservations before selected/extracted source-output, RGB, upload and replacement buffer work. Retained CPU diagnostic/rank charges use actual vector capacity; live textures use four logical bytes per texel. Replacements include existing retained charges until publication. Regional XYZ includes row/full-XY virtual fallback estimates; range scans reserve a full-plane output before IO. Stable render hits acquire no new reservations. Document/context teardown releases corresponding charges. Lower limits are validated before preference publication. Invalid values, failed writes and below-live limits preserve settings.",
  "boundaries": "Reservations are conservative managed quantities, not measured physical memory. Borrowed source outputs may be charged again; the separate XY cache remains independent. Provider/codec/transform/compositor internals, font/annotation/GUI metadata, other dialogs/previews, allocator and driver overhead remain external. New scene allocation is refused rather than evicting live GPU objects. Historical peak reservations may exceed a subsequently lowered limit.",
  "verification": "5010 selected Python checks per OS (4431 base including nine new resource tests, plus 579 channel tests); twelve native suites, eight session groups, three desktop IO/startup/append suites, 36 rank-host cases / 499 checks and two resource groups per OS. Three hidden/recreated GL contexts cover canvas reuse and the new memory reservations. Memory tests verify reservation transfer/release/overflow, pre-provider denial for ordinary/XYZ views, exact 8388608/8486912-byte diagnostic retention, live-limit refusal without mutation, stable-frame reuse, diagnostic teardown and pre-read GL reservations/texture teardown. ImGui recovery errors fail the GL check. Fresh installed SDK consumers check the new 1024 MiB setting; channel tests use proper disposable installed origins and byte-identical modules. Readers verify 296 existing reports / 39261 raw input frames; all 1297 registrations stay unchanged. No complete ImageJ/Fiji source/reference/resource/real-GPU/OS-desktop/platform acceptance.",
